  "_comment": "Turnstile contract, replayed by the Kotlin and JavaScript ports against their own hand-ported UsageClient. The behaviour is desert-ant-core's Sources/Usage/UsageClient.swift, which the Swift SDK uses directly rather than porting, and which replays this file too (Tests/UsageTests/UsageVectorTests.swift). See packages/tongue-node/USAGE.md. Flat parallel arrays, no nested objects, so both ports read it with the same minimal reader they use for the model vectors instead of taking a JSON dependency. sendCounts uses -1 for an omitted callCount, and the emit days (UTC days since the epoch) use -1 for state written before the day was stored. A 'relaunch' step replaces the client over the same state, as a new process would. Epochs are realistic on purpose: the emit days are UTC days of the clock, and the day-crossing cases sit on a real UTC midnight.",
